  "Question": "If \\(a\\) is parallel to \\(b\\) in a plane, but \\(a\\) itself also lies in this plane, what is the conclusion?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "It is still parallel",
    "B": "It must be perpendicular",
    "C": "We cannot say that \\(a\\) is parallel to the plane",
    "D": "\\(a\\) is a skew line"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "A line lying in a plane is not considered “parallel to the plane.” Parallelism requires having no points in common.",
